  "description": "The :646-652 WHEN OTHER arm of READNEXT-TRANSACT-FILE, forced to strike AFTER the browse has been positioned and one row painted. The failure sets WS-ERR-FLG, so the IF at :299 is false and the row is not painted, and the loop at :297 exits on ERR-FLG-ON with WS-IDX at two. Control takes the ELSE at :314 - not because of end-of-file but because of the error flag, since :305 tests BOTH conditions - so NEXT-PAGE-NO is set and, WS-IDX (2) being greater than one, :317-318 bumps the page number to one. The screen is then sent a second time at :326 even though the read failed, because :283's guard was passed before the failure occurred. That is the behaviour, and it is why the send count is two rather than one as in case07. MAIN-PARA's first-entry branch performs BOTH PROCESS-ENTER-KEY at :115 AND SEND-TRNLST-SCREEN at :116, so this path sends one more time than PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD does on its own - the last send is :116's and it re-paints the same screen with WS-MESSAGE unchanged.",
